---
import BookLayout from "../../layouts/BookLayout.astro";
import BookBlocks from "../../components/BookBlocks.astro";
import book from "../../data/book.json";
import { groupBookRows, loadBookSync, loadCurriculumRows, loadManifestInfo, loadManuscriptRows } from "../../lib/book-status";
import { orangeRevision } from "../../data/orange-sources";
const info = loadManifestInfo();
const curriculumGroups = groupBookRows(loadCurriculumRows(book.chapters));
const manuscriptGroups = groupBookRows(loadManuscriptRows(book.chapters));
const sync = loadBookSync();
---

<BookLayout>
  <div class="book-introduction">
    <img src="/projects/orange/book-cover.svg" alt="The Orange Book cover: the Orange emblem in cream on an orange field." width="1600" height="2400" />
    <div>
      <p>This site hosts two drafts. Neither is a finished book.</p>
      <p>The pages here are the earlier manuscript, <a href={book.sourceUrl}>docs/THE_ORANGE_BOOK.md</a>: the original 17-chapter text plus appendices. It is an earlier draft. Chapter numbers stay as they are until one renumbering pass later. This is not the Novice, Journeyman, and Master curriculum.</p>
      <p class="book-introduction-note">That curriculum is a separate work in docs/book/, being written now. It is not these pages, and it is not complete. These pages are also not a normative specification, proof, assurance report, license grant, or release claim.</p>
      <span class="book-edition">Pre-alpha reader guide</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <BookBlocks
    blockTag="h2"
    variant="contents"
    curriculumGroups={curriculumGroups}
    manuscriptGroups={manuscriptGroups}
    version={info.version}
    sync={sync}
  />

  <section class="book-checks" aria-labelledby="book-checks-title">
    <h2 id="book-checks-title">How the hosted chapters are checked</h2>
    <p>The hosted chapters are manuscript {book.version}, snapshot {book.snapshot}, revision {book.revision}. The site checks that text against the vendored manuscript. That check is not a new compiler run. The SHA-256 reference fixture is compiler/fixtures/s3b/valid-sha256-functions.or. compiler/crates/orangec/tests/s3b_conformance.rs expects sha256::round0_a = 0x5d6aebcd. A fixture result is not a proof or a security claim. Compiler sentences on this site were checked against orange main {orangeRevision} on 9 October 2026, a later revision than this manuscript. Compiler tests were not re-run.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="book-start">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/book/preface/">Start the manuscript <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </p>
</BookLayout>
